Branches: Down-Up Transition

Purpose:
  Defines the bidirectional transition protocol for task execution.
  DOWN (top-down) for execution; UP (bottom-up) for verification.
  WORK descends from MODUL → CASE → TASK → SUBTASK; VERIFICATION
  ascends SUBTASK → TASK → CASE → MODUL.
  Every level must close before the level above it can advance.

Owns: branches/DOWN-UP-TRANSITION.sdd

## DOWN — Execution Flow (top-down)

Down_Flow:
    MODUL → CASE → TASK → SUBTASK

  MODUL:
    parent: main
    purpose: Module development branch (bounded context)
    example: MODUL/auth, MODUL/payment

  CASE:
    parent: MODUL/<module>
    purpose: Business capability specification
    example: CASE_02_03 (Escrow Calculation)

  TASK:
    parent: CASE/<case>
    purpose: Concrete implementation work item
    example: TASK-PAYMENT-003

  SUBTASK:
    parent: TASK/<task>
    purpose: Smallest unit of change
    example: SUBTASK-PAYMENT-003-01
    schema: @../schemas/subtask.sdd (mini execution contract per unit)
    lifecycle: @../tasks/SUBTASK-STATE-MACHINE.sdd
      (TODO -> IN_PROGRESS -> IMPLEMENTED -> CR_REVIEW -> REFACTORED ->
       SECURITY_REVIEW -> TESTING -> PASSED -> DONE; rework loops and
       BLOCKED semantics defined there)

  Rule: Work always begins at the MODUL level and descends.
  Rule: Each level owns its child — changes do not cross sibling boundaries.

## UP — Verification Flow (bottom-up)

Up_Flow:
    SUBTASK → TASK → CASE → MODUL

  Subtask_Verify:
    - Unit lifecycle reached PASSED (all unit gates green — bax
      ../tasks/SUBTASK-STATE-MACHINE.sdd)
    - Done proof complete (bax ../tasks/DONE-PROOF.sdd)

  Task_Verify:
    - All subtasks verified
    - Integration tests pass

  Case_Verify:
    - All tasks verified
    - BDD scenarios pass

  Module_Verify:
    - All cases verified
    - Module-level integration tests pass

  Rule: A level CANNOT advance until ALL children at the level below are verified.
  Rule: This is the generalized form of the CHAIN-004 fix for competing ownership claims.

## Down-Up Relationship

Relationship:
    Work flows DOWN (execution).
    Verification flows UP (closing).

  In short: WORK flows top-down, VERIFICATION returns bottom-up.

  Example:
    1. MODUL/payment branch created
    2. CASE_02_03 spec defined
    3. TASK-PAYMENT-003 and SUBTASKs planned
    4. [DOWN] Implement SUBTASK → TASK → CASE
    5. [UP] Verify SUBTASK → TASK → CASE → MODUL
    6. Merge ready at MODUL level

## Verification Rules

Verify_Rules:
  [DU1] Every subtask MUST be verified before its parent task.
  [DU2] Every task MUST be verified before its parent case.
  [DU3] Every case MUST be verified before its parent module.
  [DU4] Verification failures MUST propagate up the tree.
  [DU5] A parent level CANNOT be marked complete until all children are verified.
  [DU6] If a child fails verification, the parent reverts to "in progress" state.

## Integration with Chain Graph

Chain_Integration:
  The chain graph (D0 → arm → D0) operates within a task scope.
  D0 is the task root — each arm executes within the current task's
  verification context.

  Arm completion → verify at task level (UP direction).
  Task completion → verify at case level (UP direction).
  Case completion → verify at module level (UP direction).

